1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,440
(Amy:)For two people who claim to be
no longer pair-bonded,

2
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:04,880
(Amy:)you spend an inordinate amount
of time in each other's company.

3
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,750
(Penny:)Yeah.

4
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:10,820
(Amy:)Dare.

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,350
(Amy:)I don't believe the rules allow

6
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:15,260
(Amy:)for an ex post facto
option change.

7
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:17,060
(Penny:)Yeah.

8
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:21,590
(Penny:)Okay, look, just because we're
not seeing each other anymore

9
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,260
(Penny:)doesn't mean
we can't be friends.

10
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:25,070
(Penny:)I mean, Leonard's a great guy.

11
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:27,270
(Amy:)Then, why did you terminate
your relationship with him?

12
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:28,640
(Bernadette:)I don't know.

13
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:31,500
(Penny:)He got really serious,
and I wasn't ready for it.

14
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:32,840
(Amy:)Interesting.

15
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,510
(Amy:)How will you react
if, in the future,

16
00:00:34,510 --> 00:00:36,610
(Amy:)you become ready for it,
and Leonard is unavailable,

17
00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:38,750
(Amy:)because another woman
has realized that he is--

18
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:41,180
(Amy:)to use your words--
"a great guy"?

19
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:45,490
(Penny:)You can only ask one question.

20
00:00:46,490 --> 00:00:48,760
(Amy and Bernadette together:)That one.

21
00:00:49,990 --> 00:00:59,020
(Bernadette:)You know what,
I don't want to play anymore.

